.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH sealtask-tasks-create 1  "SealTask CLI 0.3.0" "SealTask Manual"
.SH NAME
sealtask\-tasks\-create \- Create an encrypted task
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsealtask tasks create\fR [\fB\-\-api\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-storage\-origin\fR] [\fB\-\-work\-list\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-body\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-body\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-edit\fR] [\fB\-\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-priority\fR] [\fB\-\-due\-at\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-due\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-at\fR] [\fB\-\-section\-id\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-section\fR] [\fB\-\-connect\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-input\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-read\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-input\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-\-request\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-retry\fR] [\fB\-\-offline\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create an encrypted task
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH TARGET
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
Project name, UUID, or unique UUID prefix
.TP
\fB\-\-work\-list\-id\fR \fI<WORK_LIST_ID>\fR
Exact project UUID (legacy compatibility)
.TP
\fB\-\-section\-id\fR \fI<SECTION_ID>\fR
Initial section UUID
.TP
\fB\-\-section\fR \fI<SECTION>\fR
Initial section name, UUID, or unique UUID prefix
.SH FIELDS
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
Plaintext task title
.TP
\fB\-\-body\fR \fI<BODY>\fR
Plaintext Markdown task body
.TP
\fB\-\-priority\fR \fI<PRIORITY>\fR
Task priority: low/p4/1, medium/p3/3, high/p2/5, or urgent/p1/8
.TP
\fB\-\-due\-at\fR \fI<DUE_AT>\fR
Due time as an RFC 3339 timestamp
.TP
\fB\-\-due\fR \fI<DUE>\fR
Human due date in the project\*(Aqs timezone (for example tomorrow or 2026\-08\-10)
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-at\fR \fI<START_AT>\fR
Start time as an RFC 3339 timestamp
.SH INPUT
.TP
\fB\-\-body\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read the plaintext Markdown task body from PATH; use \*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdin
.TP
\fB\-\-input\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read the complete camelCase task input object from a UTF\-8 JSON file
.TP
\fB\-\-input\-stdin\fR
Read the complete camelCase task input object from stdin
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the account password from stdin when no local unlock is available
.SH INTERACTION
.TP
\fB\-\-edit\fR
Open your configured editor; \-\-title, \-\-body, and \-\-body\-file seed its contents
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; fail with an actionable validation error when input is missing
.SH ADVANCED
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fI<IDEMPOTENCY_KEY>\fR
Stable retry key containing at most 128 ASCII letters, digits, \*(Aq.\*(Aq, \*(Aq_\*(Aq, \*(Aq\-\*(Aq, or \*(Aq:\*(Aq
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Resolve, validate, and encrypt the request but do not create the task
.SH CONNECTION
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-url\fR \fI<API_URL>\fR [default: https://sealtask.com]
SealTask API base URL
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_API_URL\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-storage\-origin\fR \fI<STORAGE_ORIGIN>\fR
Trusted origin for presigned attachment transfers (repeatable)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_STORAGE_ORIGINS\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-connect\-timeout\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
Maximum time to establish a control\-plane connection (for example 5s)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_CONNECT_TIMEOUT\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-read\-timeout\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
Maximum idle time while reading a control\-plane response (for example 30s)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_READ_TIMEOUT\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-request\-timeout\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
Maximum total time for one control\-plane request (for example 1m)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_REQUEST_TIMEOUT\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-retry\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR [default: 2]
Retry replay\-safe API requests after transient failures
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_RETRY\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Read only from the encrypted local snapshot and never access the network
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_OFFLINE\fR environment variable.
.RE
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit compact JSON instead of human\-readable output
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Select human\-readable, finite JSON, or streaming JSON Lines output
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
json\-pretty
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Control colors in human\-readable output
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_COLOR\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-pager\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Control paging of long human\-readable output
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_PAGER_MODE\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Disable paging (equivalent to \-\-pager never)
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Control delayed progress indicators on stderr
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_PROGRESS\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress automatic paging, progress, and successful mutation acknowledgements
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Emit redacted operator telemetry to stderr; repeat for more detail
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Emit maximum redacted diagnostic telemetry to stderr
.SH PROFILE
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Isolate credentials and unlock state under a named profile
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_PROFILE\fR environment variable.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Override the base directory used for credentials and local unlock state
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEALTASK_CONFIG_DIR\fR environment variable.
.RE
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  sealtask tasks create \-\-edit
  sealtask tasks create \-\-title "Ship 0.4" \-\-due tomorrow
  sealtask tasks create \-\-project Release \-\-section Doing \-\-priority high \-\-title "Publish artifacts"
  sealtask tasks create \-\-input\-file ./task.json
  sealtask \-\-json tasks create \-\-input\-file ./task.json \-\-dry\-run
